<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#10182c">
  <title>Molecule Mission — States of Matter</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <main class="game">
    <div class="topline">
      <div class="brand">✦ Molecule Mission</div>
      <div class="mission-count" id="missionCount">Mission 1 of 3</div>
    </div>
    <h1>Change the state.<br>Complete the mission.</h1>
    <p class="intro">Heat or cool your sample and watch its molecules transform. Can you guide matter through all three states?</p>

    <section class="layout" aria-label="Molecule Mission game">
      <div class="panel sample-panel">
        <div class="sample-heading">
          <span class="eyebrow">Your sample · water</span>
          <span class="state-pill" id="statePill"><span class="state-dot"></span><span id="stateLabel">Liquid</span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="canvas-wrap">
          <canvas id="gameCanvas" role="group" tabindex="0" aria-label="Animated water molecules. Use the arrow keys to select a molecule, then Enter or Space to highlight it."></canvas>
        </div>
        <div class="canvas-caption">
          <span id="particleCaption">Molecules slide past one another</span>
          <span>Click or tap a molecule · focus here and use arrow keys</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="panel control-panel" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="eyebrow mission-label">Current mission</div>
        <h2 id="missionTitle">Freeze the sample</h2>
        <p class="mission-copy" id="missionCopy">Cool the water until it becomes a solid. Aim for 0°C or colder.</p>

        <div class="thermometer">
          <div class="thermometer-heading">
            <span class="eyebrow">Temperature</span>
            <span class="temperature"><span id="temperature">22</span><small> °C</small></span>
          </div>
          <div class="scale" aria-hidden="true"><span class="scale-marker" id="scaleMarker"></span></div>
          <div class="scale-labels"><span>−40°C</span><span>0°C</span><span>100°C</span><span>140°C</span></div>
          <p class="phase-note" id="phaseNote">Water is liquid between 0°C and 100°C.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="eyebrow control-label">Adjust the temperature</div>
        <div class="temperature-controls">
          <button class="control-button" id="coolButton" type="button" aria-label="Cool by 5 degrees">❄ Cool −5°</button>
          <button class="control-button" id="heatButton" type="button" aria-label="Heat by 5 degrees">☀ Heat +5°</button>
        </div>
        <button class="submit-button" id="submitButton" type="button">Lock in this state</button>
        <p class="feedback" id="feedback" role="status">Tip: hold a temperature button to change it faster.</p>
        <button class="restart-button hidden" id="restartButton" type="button">Play again</button>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="learn" aria-label="States of matter facts">
      <article class="fact solid"><h3>Solid</h3><p>Molecules vibrate in fixed positions and keep their shape.</p></article>
      <article class="fact liquid"><h3>Liquid</h3><p>Molecules stay close but slide around; liquids take their container’s shape.</p></article>
      <article class="fact gas"><h3>Gas</h3><p>Molecules spread out and zip freely to fill their container.</p></article>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script src="./script.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>